	{
		"title": "Levels, and why they barely matter",
		"kind": "text",
		"request": "level = warning(1) or fatal(2)",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "In TLS 1.3 only close_notify and user_canceled are warnings. Every other description is fatal regardless of the byte, and closes the connection.",
		"response_hex": "",
		"note": "Do not decide what to do from the level byte — decide from the description. A peer that sends handshake_failure at level 1 is still telling you the handshake is over.",
